txtql::eval::repeated_key

  ⚠ key `set-cookie` is set more than once; the later value wins
   ╭─[query.tql:2:32]
 1 │ -- Without LISTOF, a repeated key keeps the later value and is reported.
 2 │ TEXT   = 1 TO n hs:header AS { LOWER(h.name): h.value FOR h IN hs }
   ·                                ──────┬──────
   ·                                      ╰── this sets the key again
 3 │ header = name:(ANY UNTIL ': ') value:(ANY UNTIL NL)
   ╰────
  help: to keep every value, collect them with `LISTOF`, e.g. `{ k: LISTOF v FOR x IN xs }`

Advice: 
  ☞ in this part of the input
   ╭─[input.txt:1:1]
 1 │ ╭─▶ Set-Cookie: a=1
 2 │ ├─▶ Set-Cookie: b=2
   · ╰──── matched text
   ╰────
